+# Fictional in-world source excerpt — M-17 Margin Register
+
+Delivery mode (R9): verbatim
+
+M-17 identifies Teva as the initial recorder and names the Slate Table as its filing place.
+Teva names the paper folio "Lorn Index" as the sheet she opened for the check.
+Orni writes on the margin: "not weighed; mark unmeasured."
+The folio identifies Teva and Orni as its two annotators.
+The inventory lists the Slate Table as the place holding the folio.
+Entry A: Teva files the Lorn Index on the Slate Table.
+Entry B: after Entry A, Orni adds "not weighed; mark unmeasured" to the Lorn Index at the Slate Table.
+The register gives no measured weight for the Lorn Index.
