+Source-version limit: the source page identifies the translator and year; its specific printed copy was not independently identified.
+Delivery mode (R9): translation
+
+> Then the whole Plain of High Heaven was obscured and all the Central Land of Reed-Plains darkened. Owing to this, eternal night prevailed.
+> Therefore did the eight hundred myriad deities assemble in a divine assembly in the bed of the Tranquil River of Heaven, […]
+> So when the Heaven-Shining-Great-August deity had come forth, both the Plain of High Heaven and the Central-Land-of-Reed-Plains of course again became light.
+
+This short translation excerpt supports only the editorial comparison rows. It is not an in-world source, not fictional canon, and does not establish the original-language wording or a general Japanese/Shinto meaning.
